&lt;h3&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Global Payroll Manager to join the growing Finance team at Nex. This is a high-impact, hands-on role for a payroll professional who thrives in a fast-paced, high-growth environment. You will build and own the global payroll function—establishing best-in-class processes, ensuring compliance across multiple jurisdictions, and serving as the company’s internal payroll authority as we expand domestically and internationally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will rationalize and optimize payroll workflows, manage relationships with international payroll providers, and ensure accurate reconciliation of payroll-related balance sheet accounts. You will partner closely with Finance, HR, Legal, and the broader business to ensure payroll operations keep pace with company growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build best-in-class global payroll processes&lt;/strong&gt;— assess current state workflows, identify gaps, and implement scalable, efficient processes for payroll execution across all applicable jurisdictions domestically and internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage international payroll providers&lt;/strong&gt;— onboard and oversee third-party payroll vendors across multiple countries, ensuring accuracy, compliance, and service quality. Serve as the primary point of contact for all payroll provider relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reconcile payroll-related balance sheet accounts&lt;/strong&gt;— own the end-to-end reconciliation of payroll-related balance sheet accounts including accrued compensation, payroll liabilities, and related accounts, ensuring accuracy and alignment with the general ledger.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure global payroll compliance&lt;/strong&gt;— maintain up-to-date knowledge of payroll regulations across applicable jurisdictions; manage registrations, filings, and remittances in accordance with local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive payroll automation and technology&lt;/strong&gt;— evaluate and implement payroll technology solutions to reduce manual effort, improve data accuracy, and streamline reporting across geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain a comprehensive payroll calendar&lt;/strong&gt;— oversee all payroll cycles, tax filings, and statutory payments, ensuring timely and accurate execution across all regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support audits and compliance reviews&lt;/strong&gt;— serve as primary contact for internal and external audits related to payroll; coordinate documentation and responses to resolve inquiries efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner cross-functionally&lt;/strong&gt;— collaborate with HR, Accounting, Legal, and FP&amp;amp;A to provide payroll guidance on new hires, equity events, benefit programs, and organizational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of progressive payroll experience, with a mix of global payroll operations and industry experience preferred; CPP or equivalent certification a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing international payroll providers&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;across multiple countries, including vendor onboarding and ongoing performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on expertise reconciling payroll-related balance sheet accounts, including accrued compensation, payroll tax liabilities, and related GL accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder’s mentality—you are comfortable creating processes and know how to prioritize in an environment where not everything is yet defined.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payroll technology platforms&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;(e.g., ADP, Workday, Rippling, or equivalent) and a track record of leveraging automation to improve efficiency and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of multi-country payroll compliance, including statutory filings, tax withholding requirements, and local employment regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, strong written and verbal communication skills, and the ability to translate complex payroll concepts for non-payroll stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at an early-stage or high-growth startup&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;is a significant plus; consumer technology, e-commerce, or hardware industry background preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
