&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with leadership to translate headcount growth plans into workspace requirements and expansion strategies, with scalable processes to ensure smooth execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead office expansion and build-out projects end-to-end — including site selection, lease negotiation, design, construction management, and move-in coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with realtors, landlords, and co-working space providers to explore options and negotiate favourable terms, and manage the bidding and vendor selection process for construction and fit-out projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate project status, timelines, and key decisions to stakeholders and US headquarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilities &amp;amp; Operations Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the workplace is fully operational, well-maintained, and compliant with local laws, building regulations, and tenancy agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own workplace safety and security, including policies, access control systems, CCTV, fire safety equipment, first-aid provisions, and emergency procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and maintain all utilities and infrastructure — electricity, water, internet, and IT/AV equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the workplace improvement backlog, prioritising based on stakeholder needs and budget, and working with vendors to execute will be ongoing responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Finance, and Operations on lease management, renewals, insurance, and business registration compliance is also essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage office administration team and be responsible for the maintenance and upkeep of workplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the workplace and facilities budget, including obtaining approvals and reviewing expenses for expansion and improvement projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect workplace requirements and feedback from employees and stakeholders to continuously improve the office experience, fostering a positive workplace culture and supporting employee productivity, as well as making decisions on workspace assignments and office improvements based on strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology &amp;amp; Infrastructure Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with corporate IT teams to ensure robust networking (ethernet, Wi-Fi), A/V systems, meeting room technology, and workplace systems (badge access, room booking, visitor management).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10 years of experience in office management, workplace operations, facilities management, or corporate real estate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of managing office expansion or build-out projects in a fast-paced, high-growth environment is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a multinational company (MNC) or tech company with exposure to multi-country operations or global standards is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You should have strong project management skills with the ability to manage multiple vendors, timelines, and stakeholders simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with lease negotiation, vendor contracting, and managing CAPEX/OPEX budgets is expected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Hong Kong building regulations, workplace safety requirements, and tenancy/lease compliance is necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to coordinate with overseas headquarters across timezones are critical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and Cantonese is required, with Mandarin being a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on, proactive mindset suited to a fast-moving startup environment is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in consumer tech, e-commerce, or high-growth startups would be valuable. Exposure to setting up new offices from scratch (greenfield projects) is beneficial.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree or certification in Facilities Management, Project Management (PMP), or related fields is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with workplace systems and tools (e.g., space booking, IWMS, access control platforms) is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
