&lt;h3 class=&quot;paragraph-3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a QA Engineer who loves games, sweats the details, and enjoys learning new technology. Motion-based QA is different from traditional game QA: you’ll test with your whole body in real-world environments (lighting, room sizes, player heights, 1–4 players, etc.). Prior motion-gaming experience is &lt;em&gt;not required&lt;/em&gt;—strong QA fundamentals and a learning mindset are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;text-block-4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and execute test plans and test cases for motion-based games and the Nex Playground experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate core player experience for living-room play: onboarding, clarity, responsiveness, and “is this fun and understandable?”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test motion-game fundamentals such as responsiveness/latency, recognition consistency, occlusion handling, and edge cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform functional, usability, regression, localization, and device/compatibility testing across the product surface area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write excellent bug reports with clear repro steps, expected vs. actual results, environment details, and short video captures when helpful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally: clarify requirements, ask good questions, and flag risk areas early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1–2 years of experience in IT or the game industry (or equivalent hands-on experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of QA methodologies, tools, and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and a commitment to quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication and teamwork skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good command of written and spoken English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on comfort with hardware and TV setups, including basic troubleshooting (network, setup flows, updates)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to perform physical movements during testing and appear in internal test recordings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in games and player experience—especially party/family-friendly titles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;text-block-4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cantonese and/or Mandarin fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing camera-based, motion, AR, or computer vision products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing multiplayer/local co-op or party games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Unity, Android-based hardware, or mobile gaming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting up consumer electronics (TVs, consoles, streaming devices).&lt;/li&gt;
