&lt;p&gt;To protect yourself from recruitment scams, please note that Nex communicates through official company emails ending in @nex.inc. If you receive a suspicious email or message, please do not respond and report it immediately to us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Hong Kong&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Type: 12-month contract (with possibility of conversion to full-time permanent role)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;paragraph-3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer in Test at Nex, you will own stability and reliability testing for the Motion Development Kit (MDK), firmware, and hardware modules that power Nex Playground&#39;s AOSP-based motion-sensing device. You will build automated test frameworks, stress/soak testing infrastructure, and validation tools that catch instability, regressions, and hardware-integration failures before they reach production. You will work closely with the Framework Engineering and firmware/hardware teams to embed testability across the full Android stack, from low-level sensor drivers and HAL layers up through the MDK APIs that game developers build on .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within a small, highly technical team that values both specialization and collaboration, with clear ownership of quality across core technology areas .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Mindset&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are drawn to solving hard reliability problems in systems where hardware, firmware, and Android software all have to work together flawlessly, day after day. You care deeply about long-run stability, not just passing a test once, but proving a system holds up under sustained load, edge cases, and real-world conditions. You thrive in environments where deep systems debugging, Android/AOSP internals knowledge, and rigorous testing discipline directly shape what the platform can confidently ship .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;text-block-4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build automated stability and reliability test frameworks for the Motion Development Kit (MDK), firmware, and hardware modules on an AOSP-based platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop soak testing, stress testing, and endurance testing pipelines to surface memory leaks, crashes, thermal issues, ANRs, and long-running failures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build test harnesses and hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) rigs to validate sensor, camera, and motion-tracking hardware under real and simulated conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create regression suites for firmware, HAL, and MDK releases, integrated into CI/CD to catch stability issues pre-release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate, reproduce, and drive root-cause analysis of field failures, crashes, kernel panics, and intermittent hardware/firmware defects using Android bug reports, logcat, and kernel logs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track reliability metrics such as MTBF, crash rates, ANR rates, and failure recurrence across hardware revisions and firmware/AOSP builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with firmware, hardware, and platform engineers to define quality gates and exit criteria for new hardware/firmware/AOSP releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-tested test code and tooling that raises the engineering bar across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and reporting for test coverage, defect trends, and release stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews and contribute to shared tools, infrastructure, and cross-role projects (20% Time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the dual-leadership model (Engineering Manager and Tech Lead) to align on quality priorities and technical direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document test strategies, systems, and findings to support team knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience in software test engineering, reliability engineering, or QA for embedded/firmware, Android, or hardware-integrated systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python, with experience in at least one systems language (C++, C#, Java, Rust, or Go)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with stability, stress, soak, or endurance testing methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing Android/AOSP platforms, HAL, embedded firmware, device drivers, or hardware modules (sensors, motion tracking, cameras, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging skills across hardware, firmware, and software layers, including logcat, kernel logs, bug reports, logic analyzers, or serial/hardware diagnostics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or maintaining CI/CD pipelines and automated regression suites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;text-block-4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;bold-text-2&quot;&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AOSP build systems (Soong/Make), Android Test Harness, or Vendor Test Suite (VTS)/Compatibility Test Suite (CTS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) test rig design and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with embedded Linux, Android kernel internals, and Treble/HAL architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of communication protocols (I2C, SPI, UART, BLE) used in sensor and firmware integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with reliability metrics and frameworks (MTBF, FMEA, fault injection testing)&lt;/li&gt;
